* Setness closure in tools/cl.py: ` negex ` for a negation and ` ovex ` for an operation value.

s1::id |- ( A e. RR -> A e. RR )
s2::negex |- -u A e. _V
s3:s2:a1i |- ( A e. RR -> -u A e. _V )
s4::ovex |- ( A + A ) e. _V
s5:s4:a1i |- ( A e. RR -> ( A + A ) e. _V )
qed:s3,s5:jca |- ( A e. RR -> ( -u A e. _V /\ ( A + A ) e. _V ) )
